  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Sound waves of different frequencies can be used in different purposes.&nbsp;FM broadcasting frequently makes use of frequency modulation. Additionally, it is utilised in telemetry, radar, seismic prospecting, EEG-based seizure monitoring of neonates, two-way radio systems, sound synthesis, magnetic tape recording, and some video transmission systems.</p><p>The range for FM broadcasting lies between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>88</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>108</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math>&nbsp;does not belong to the FM broadcast.</p>",
    "image": null
